# Security Policy 

## Supported versions 

DevPulse is an actively developed project. Security fixes are primarily 
applied to the current development version. 

Older versions may not receive security updates. 

## Reporting a vulnerability 

Please do not report security vulnerabilities through public GitHub issues. 

If you discover a vulnerability, please contact the project maintainer 
privately through the security contact or private reporting mechanism 
provided by the repository. 

Please include: 
- A description of the vulnerability.
- Steps to reproduce the issue.
- The affected component or version.
- The potential security impact.
- Any suggested mitigation, if available.

Please avoid including real credentials, private telemetry, personal data,
or other sensitive information in a report. 

## Scope 

Security reports are particularly relevant to: 

- Authentication and authorization.
- API endpoints.
- Telemetry and stored monitoring data.
- Database access. - AI/API integrations.
- Secret and credential handling.
- Dependency vulnerabilities.
- Client/server data boundaries.

## Responsible disclosure

Please allow reasonable time for the issue to be investigated and, where 
appropriate, fixed before publicly disclosing technical details. 

The project maintainer may acknowledge valid security reports after the issue 
has been investigated and resolved.
